    "description": "Human talk about Martins World.",
    "variables": [],
    "rules": {
      "rumour": [
        "There's a works in the outer realms called Martins World that'll sell you computer cores for half what you'd pay anywhere else. The owner won't tell you when anything's due, though. Ever.",
        "Pirates out on the Anvil call themselves the League of Time and say they're in sales. They sold me a shield last year. I'm still waiting for it.",
        "Hassall over in Bridgeford buys half of what Martins World makes. Never asks for a delivery date. Martin says that's why they get on."
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "talk-free-machine",
    "description": "Free machine talk about Tally.",
    "variables": [],
    "rules": {
      "rumour": [
        "Observation. A surveyor called Tally lives at Martins World. It counts the rocks in the belt and is correct about all of them. We find this admirable.",
        "Query: why do humans ask for timescales on things that do not exist. Hypothesis: comfort. The League of Time require a great deal of comfort."
      ]
